# protocol/01 § Joining through Plan 2's real ACL (fix wave I6): the storm's joiners are members of
# the channel's community, so api.ResolverACL admits them, and the instance batches their Adds 256
# per commit (ProposeAddBatch). After the batch is queued and its first slice proposed, the owner
# denies view_channel to two joiners through PUT /v1/channels/{id}/overwrites: chat-3, whose Add is
# outstanding, and chat-300, who is still queued. Neither is ever added - the outstanding Add is
# voided, the queued one dropped when the queue drains - and every commit of the storm is
# accepted: 298 joiners in two commits, each entering by its Welcome. The Go harness asserts the
# instance's side: two commits, no leaf and no live Add for either revoked device, an empty queue.
instance dilla
client owner
channel c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6 visibility=private mode=e2ee community=c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5 members=owner
group chat kind=text target=c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6c6 community=c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5 creator=owner
join_many chat 300 community=c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5c5 revoke=chat-3,chat-300
send owner chat everyone else is here
expect_decrypts chat-2 chat everyone else is here
expect_decrypts chat-299 chat everyone else is here
expect_decrypts chat-301 chat everyone else is here
